nocked the baton from Jackson’s hand. To her credit, Jackson caught the baton on the bounce, and ran on, but the delay proved disastrous, and Australia could only finish fifth. Germany then had the lead at the start of the anchor leg, but " [:a {:href "/athletes/77857"} "Cathy Hardy"] " (USA) gained two metres to edge out " [:a {:href "/athletes/70074"} "Marga Petersen"] " of Germany, both teams running world records of 45.9 – although the automatic time had the US with 46.14 to 46.18 for Germany."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77881"} "Barbara Jones"] " ran the second leg for the United States, aged only 15 years, 123 days on the day of the final. Through 2024, she remains the youngest athlete, male or female, to have won an Olympic athletics gold medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "46.5 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "45.9 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/77820"} "Mae Faggs"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77881"} "Barbara Jones"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77919"} "Janet Moreau"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77857"} "Cathy Hardy"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/923350"} "Mary McNabb"] [:small {} " (DNS)"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77798"} "Connie Darnowski"] [:small {} " (DNS)"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77815"} "Dolores Dwyer"] [:small {} " (DNS)"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77894"} "Mabel Landry"] [:small {} " (DNS)"]]] [:tr {: